    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n\\n#pragma STDC FP_CONTRACT OFF\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\nstatic void *aligned_malloc(size_t size) {\\n    void *ptr = NULL;\\n    if (posix_memalign(&ptr, 64, size) != 0) return NULL;\\n    return ptr;\\n}\\n\\nvoid body_force(float * restrict px, float * restrict py, float * restrict pz,\\n                float * restrict vx, float * restrict vy, float * restrict vz,\\n                int n) {\\n    const float dt = DT;\\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n    for (int i0 = 0; i0 < n; i0 += 4) {\\n        if (i0 + 3 < n) {\\n            // Vectorized group of 4\\n            float32x4_t x_i = vld1q_f32(px + i0);\\n            float32x4_t y_i = vld1q_f32(py + i0);\\n            float32x4_t z_i = vld1q_f32(pz + i0);\\n            float32x4_t fx = vdupq_n_f32(0.0f);\\n            float32x4_t fy = vdupq_n_f32(0.0f);\\n            float32x4_t fz = vdupq_n_f32(0.0f);\\n\\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n                float pxj = px[j];\\n                float pyj = py[j];\\n                float pzj = pz[j];\\n\\n                float32x4_t dx = vsubq_f32(vdupq_n_f32(pxj), x_i);\\n                float32x4_t dy = vsubq_f32(vdupq_n_f32(pyj), y_i);\\n                float32x4_t dz = vsubq_f32(vdupq_n_f32(pzj), z_i);\\n\\n                float32x4_t dx2 = vmulq_f32(dx, dx);\\n                float32x4_t dy2 = vmulq_f32(dy, dy);\\n                float32x4_t dz2 = vmulq_f32(dz, dz);\\n                float32x4_t sqrd = vaddq_f32(vaddq_f32(vaddq_f32(dx2, dy2), dz2),\\n                                             vdupq_n_f32(SOFTENING));\\n\\n                float32x4_t inv_dist = vdivq_f32(vdupq_n_f32(1.0f), vsqrtq_f32(sqrd));\\n                float32x4_t inv_dist3 = vmulq_f32(vmulq_f32(inv_dist, inv_dist), inv_dist);\\n\\n                fx = vaddq_f32(fx, vmulq_f32(dx, inv_dist3));\\n                fy = vaddq_f32(fy, vmulq_f32(dy, inv_dist3));\\n                fz = vaddq_f32(fz, vmulq_f32(dz, inv_dist3));\\n            }\\n\\n            float32x4_t dvx = vmulq_n_f32(fx, dt);\\n            float32x4_t dvy = vmulq_n_f32(fy, dt);\\n            float32x4_t dvz = vmulq_n_f32(fz, dt);\\n\\n            vst1q_f32(vx + i0, vaddq_f32(vld1q_f32(vx + i0), dvx));\\n            vst1q_f32(vy + i0, vaddq_f32(vld1q_f32(vy + i0), dvy));\\n            vst1q_f32(vz + i0, vaddq_f32(vld1q_f32(vz + i0), dvz));\\n        } else {\\n            // Scalar tail\\n            for (int i = i0; i < n; ++i) {\\n                float fx = 0.0f, fy = 0.0f, fz = 0.0f;\\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n                    float dx = px[j] - px[i];\\n                    float dy = py[j] - py[i];\\n                    float dz = pz[j] - pz[i];\\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n                    fx += dx * inv_dist3;\\n                    fy += dy * inv_dist3;\\n                    fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n                }\\n                vx[i] += dt*fx;\\n                vy[i] += dt*fy;\\n                vz[i] += dt*fz;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n    int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n    Body *tmp = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n    b = fread(tmp, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n    return tmp;\\n}\\n\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n    int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n    int nbodies;\\n    Body *tmp = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n    // Allocate aligned SoA arrays\\n    float *px = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n    float *py = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n    float *pz = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n    float *vx = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n    float *vy = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n    float *vz = (float*)aligned_malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n\\n    if (!px || !py || !pz || !vx || !vy || !vz) {\\n        fprintf(stderr, \\\"Memory allocation failed\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n        px[i] = tmp[i].x;\\n        py[i] = tmp[i].y;\\n        pz[i] = tmp[i].z;\\n        vx[i] = tmp[i].vx;\\n        vy[i] = tmp[i].vy;\\n        vz[i] = tmp[i].vz;\\n    }\\n    free(tmp);\\n\\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n        body_force(px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz, nbodies);\\n\\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n            px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\\n            py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\\n            pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Convert back to AoS for output\\n    Body *out = (Body*)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n    if (!out) { fprintf(stderr, \\\"Memory allocation failed\\\\n\\\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n        out[i].x = px[i];\\n        out[i].y = py[i];\\n        out[i].z = pz[i];\\n        out[i].vx = vx[i];\\n        out[i].vy = vy[i];\\n        out[i].vz = vz[i];\\n    }\\n\\n    write_dataset(nbodies, out);\\n\\n    free(out);\\n    free(px); free(py); free(pz); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\\n\\n    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Manual NEON vectorization across four bodies per iteration preserves the exact floating-point reduction order for each body while enabling SIMD throughput on ARM64, improving performance over compiler auto-vectorization.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Converted to SoA with 64-byte alignment. The inner j-loop processes groups of four i-bodies using NEON intrinsics; each lane performs exactly the same sequence of IEEE operations as the original scalar code (left-associative additions, no FMA contraction via #pragma STDC FP_CONTRACT OFF). OpenMP parallelization over i-blocks is retained. Scalar tail handles non-multiple-of-4 counts.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Converted AoS layout to SoA with aligned allocation\",\n    \"Replaced scalar inner loop in body_force with manual NEON intrinsics processing four bodies at a time, preserving per-body summation order and IEEE operation sequence\",\n    \"Added #pragma STDC FP_CONTRACT OFF to prevent FMA contraction that could alter results\",\n    \"Kept OpenMP parallelization over i blocks\"\n  ]\n}",
    "thinking": "We need to propose one bounded HPC source-code experiment. Role B: legal SIMD/vectorization and loop dependencies. We have current source src/nbody.c. Need to improve performance on ARM64, 4 cores, OpenMP. Baseline ~0.671s, best so far ~0.155s (experiment 6be2b0550d04446e score 0.8117). Our role history includes many attempts. We need propose one candidate.\n\nWe must edit only src/nbody.c. Need to preserve correctness exactly (binary output bytes match reference). The program reads binary input: first int nbodies, then array of Body structs each with six floats. It runs N_ITER=10 iterations: body_force computes forces and updates velocities; then positions updated.\n\nCurrent code uses OpenMP parallel for on outer i loop in body_force, schedule(static), and also parallel for position update. The inner j loop is sequential per thread. This preserves floating-point order? Actually each i's reduction over j is sequential, so results identical to serial (assuming same order). Parallelizing outer loop doesn't change per-body sum order.\n\nWe need improve SIMD/vectorization. On ARM64 with NEON, we can try to vectorize inner j loop across multiple bodies? But that would change floating-point operation order and likely break exact output comparison because reference is sequential serial code (probably compiled without OpenMP). The correctness check compares exact bytes against official reference which runs the original sequential implementation. So any reordering of floating-point operations could produce different rounding, causing mismatch. Therefore we must preserve exactly the same sequence of arithmetic operations per body as the original serial code.\n\nOriginal serial: for each i, compute fx,fy,fz by summing over j in order 0..n-1 using dx = p[j].x - p[i].x etc., then inv_dist3 computed from sqrd_dist. Then update velocities. So we must keep that exact per-i reduction order and arithmetic.\n\nThus SIMD across i (multiple bodies) would reorder? If we